[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-80492"] :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=1,$ $x=2,$ and the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=2{x}^{2}.$ What is ${∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,dA$ expressed as a repeated integral?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/4fec059132b7bd02cb64f864b6982c0c64a66c22646334ca199fad12097ba435.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 2{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186134233 :question/answer-fields 17592186131840] {:db/id "q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609/fe23525b4be0b5f64a475ec4cf5543fd02c54f70cdce7ec9d25819b7c7f12563" :answer/id #uuid "8ab606c0-b89c-5943-b0fd-a198c82279d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609/80451e930ee131aebc2fd76ba2082e2658eeb45d2ff36031dfbfdfaf7c3a4ddb" :answer/id #uuid "71a8ebde-d4a5-599a-bc49-21762635a32b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609/77ce98fec50d7e8cd2cd51184f76a9236293cebfcf167daee997577dcd6bcac7" :answer/id #uuid "18af1db1-b3c3-5c97-8e0b-ae8e1eee4c07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609/44a6bcbb3b2b9c7f8e72e7eda57798084f37fffeb589f556a24219a803da511c" :answer/id #uuid "ba3a60b0-13ed-5c52-89d6-f4478308adad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609/f41a7b7f3a8984e0799ebe5b3510ca5786e27ffe4a8713686a684cee9ac59041" :answer/id #uuid "c4b10608-a519-5016-bcc8-d5e4a26f29c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609" :answer-field/id #uuid "55441e90-a173-5241-872b-ec3620137f35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609/f41a7b7f3a8984e0799ebe5b3510ca5786e27ffe4a8713686a684cee9ac59041" :answer-field/choices ["q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609/fe23525b4be0b5f64a475ec4cf5543fd02c54f70cdce7ec9d25819b7c7f12563" "q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609/80451e930ee131aebc2fd76ba2082e2658eeb45d2ff36031dfbfdfaf7c3a4ddb" "q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609/77ce98fec50d7e8cd2cd51184f76a9236293cebfcf167daee997577dcd6bcac7" "q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609/44a6bcbb3b2b9c7f8e72e7eda57798084f37fffeb589f556a24219a803da511c" "q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609/f41a7b7f3a8984e0799ebe5b3510ca5786e27ffe4a8713686a684cee9ac59041"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-40727"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/0e05b575c22c78000a1ec235bb82cbfad3cd0cdfc6db370f19f094799b305949.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=2{x}^{2}$ and $y=1+{x}^{2},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/da2895c09bc33f628626257b6d102e74875825df14ba744904e02ffa71552a02.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40727/selection/ma-v1/a91317e819a96a969d34cf8972394ce4334a4ade404b5e2e1d33c5d5a4113609"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-81329/selection/4d9fe404a177ab9f0111f4ae5d148fc5380f16c1b40a24d393c9b63572f2f284" :answer/id #uuid "a1d022b7-4e49-51d6-8fc8-e9cf478b90a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{4x+6}^{2{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81329/selection/34a0ecaf6bd2afdfe44868a4f01346ef8f0465d19f35474115b3fc2a6e25c842" :answer/id #uuid "06b3ad92-f6e1-5413-8de5-4617cc8e7e5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{4x+6}^{2{x}^{2}}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81329/selection/86d5b186d5f5c97afba1ab0a406fc51d32f11bbf074c72cbc617246d8751eebc" :answer/id #uuid "e014ce7a-04b8-5a29-a85c-9f17f18a95bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{4x+6}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81329/selection/6b58d0d389df43e08527ff73d0499166af842c561b0e9c9dd90576feb79c3cec" :answer/id #uuid "0b3b5121-869a-598f-9e25-460313108d99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{4x+6}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81329/selection/5b184f6b7f0d5008d5f1d3cd7fcc68d00c6a4b0b73b98564aefcaf9b71326b8a" :answer/id #uuid "57b3bd96-ebe1-5590-9529-19f4d168eed0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{4x+6}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81329/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc4a6fc5-395e-5567-92b7-fc6f7ebe859d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81329/selection/6b58d0d389df43e08527ff73d0499166af842c561b0e9c9dd90576feb79c3cec" :answer-field/choices ["q-81329/selection/4d9fe404a177ab9f0111f4ae5d148fc5380f16c1b40a24d393c9b63572f2f284" "q-81329/selection/34a0ecaf6bd2afdfe44868a4f01346ef8f0465d19f35474115b3fc2a6e25c842" "q-81329/selection/86d5b186d5f5c97afba1ab0a406fc51d32f11bbf074c72cbc617246d8751eebc" "q-81329/selection/6b58d0d389df43e08527ff73d0499166af842c561b0e9c9dd90576feb79c3cec" "q-81329/selection/5b184f6b7f0d5008d5f1d3cd7fcc68d00c6a4b0b73b98564aefcaf9b71326b8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81329" :question/id #uuid "4214061a-ab7b-587e-ac5a-07f10e2cd53c" :question/math-academy-id "q-81329" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=-1,$ $x=0,$ $y=4x+6,$ and the curve $y=2{x}^{2}.$ What is ${∬}_{D}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dA$ expressed as a repeated integral?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/5d56dfdb75870a251f1eb94f0305a083489ce9e8dc4b9843138cd8ef88da30ab.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 4x+6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{4x+6}\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+y}}{y+1}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81329/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e891363-fea2-5de4-9bbb-67fddb077200"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81329"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132124/selection/523dfec636f7c6e99c37c5ee4160c7c3449ec2281ca577b88e67c39b3d4b365a" :answer/id #uuid "9afc7218-1e33-5b2a-b9d7-f2ca32bbd05e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{4}^{8}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2x}}^{2\\sqrt{x-4}}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132124/selection/4a00bea12bcbc68da74815071035d216b4de4ddc44dcc1fe96b3cacad3737cf3" :answer/id #uuid "2592a490-89bb-5c48-b3fe-80efdde843ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{4}^{\\sqrt{2x}}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x-4}}^{8}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132124/selection/05d1b535d9a3c83e5219327b1a57beff7a46368f28181949906a7e895fa8ef3b" :answer/id #uuid "e1e2601c-e30a-51df-a6de-6c3851c7679c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x-4}}^{8}{\\int }_{4}^{\\sqrt{2x}}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132124/selection/f6f9d2ffb40b4f71a66c9ebb054bd3a0f28634ac00f5db0a50014df5f7903c80" :answer/id #uuid "033d4f6a-c6f9-5b2d-9b02-972e903f6bd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x-4}}^{\\sqrt{2x}}{\\int }_{4}^{8}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132124/selection/7e4c8a2d4eee9ea9df04690a4eff2795054981bfd96a18b095f28a20d0f9b4e9" :answer/id #uuid "faee62f5-7af3-52c2-9fcd-1e94cc3c8df5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{4}^{8}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x-4}}^{\\sqrt{2x}}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132124/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9c6681b-daa8-537b-89af-62d3affd2790" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132124/selection/7e4c8a2d4eee9ea9df04690a4eff2795054981bfd96a18b095f28a20d0f9b4e9" :answer-field/choices ["q-132124/selection/523dfec636f7c6e99c37c5ee4160c7c3449ec2281ca577b88e67c39b3d4b365a" "q-132124/selection/4a00bea12bcbc68da74815071035d216b4de4ddc44dcc1fe96b3cacad3737cf3" "q-132124/selection/05d1b535d9a3c83e5219327b1a57beff7a46368f28181949906a7e895fa8ef3b" "q-132124/selection/f6f9d2ffb40b4f71a66c9ebb054bd3a0f28634ac00f5db0a50014df5f7903c80" "q-132124/selection/7e4c8a2d4eee9ea9df04690a4eff2795054981bfd96a18b095f28a20d0f9b4e9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132124" :question/id #uuid "e98de7f4-1849-55a0-92ab-57809365e833" :question/math-academy-id "q-132124" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=4,$ $x=8,$ and the curves $y=\\sqrt{2x}$ and $y=2\\sqrt{x-4}.$ What is ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dA$ expressed as a repeated integral?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/14b4aa0c290ef70b8442c5e5176c3311f9968b7a774b52a6a2472c356f190866.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,4\\le x\\le 8,\\,2\\sqrt{x-4}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{2x}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dA & ={\\int }_{4}^{8}{\\int }_{2\\sqrt{x-4}}^{\\sqrt{2x}}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132124/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e891363-fea2-5de4-9bbb-67fddb077200"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132124"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80634/selection/34c6b4db6405bf5658f1e41a378722038a0b2b966b60c2c42cc842fb62a0694b" :answer/id #uuid "f359cd06-be10-5902-ac00-bac334b0ed31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{2(x-2)^{2}-1}^{2-(x-2)^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80634/selection/da3d8e016db9b3343955ebafb8c81eef613848f6ec07f943051c9b366d96d909" :answer/id #uuid "21dace07-f103-5a54-9bf1-b2558e4919b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{2-(x-2)^{2}}^{2(x-2)^{2}-1}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80634/selection/a8d49f0a85f875f33fdd7cf19c71d070538f235f54d19bcd64e02591e62b631e" :answer/id #uuid "5464b05e-378e-5968-849b-45a5eeabfcc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{2(x-2)^{2}}^{(x-2)^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80634/selection/032aa99d69be1725dd20a58588fafcbc45e86ee05d1e74b3913dd4d7a597f238" :answer/id #uuid "db9b5411-3bbe-5d92-abd0-ea615e62c02c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2(x-2)^{2}-1}^{2-(x-2)^{2}}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80634/selection/50daa511ea438b1665c3727f3caf64a20fa9eeeacd7b55209436370197b21934" :answer/id #uuid "77196d11-2c7f-50ec-aa6c-fc75112add34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}-1}^{2+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80634/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3070a20d-c66c-55f1-960b-c5d09b457208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80634/selection/34c6b4db6405bf5658f1e41a378722038a0b2b966b60c2c42cc842fb62a0694b" :answer-field/choices ["q-80634/selection/34c6b4db6405bf5658f1e41a378722038a0b2b966b60c2c42cc842fb62a0694b" "q-80634/selection/da3d8e016db9b3343955ebafb8c81eef613848f6ec07f943051c9b366d96d909" "q-80634/selection/a8d49f0a85f875f33fdd7cf19c71d070538f235f54d19bcd64e02591e62b631e" "q-80634/selection/032aa99d69be1725dd20a58588fafcbc45e86ee05d1e74b3913dd4d7a597f238" "q-80634/selection/50daa511ea438b1665c3727f3caf64a20fa9eeeacd7b55209436370197b21934"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80634" :question/id #uuid "791269bd-c71d-54eb-974f-e94bc28e8f5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80634" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/a51b5dca6436e6ffd3af0d1cfa801141d97e7660e6218344011a5ac965c722c6.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=2(x-2)^{2}-1$ and $y=2-(x-2)^{2},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/a15535c1eee33018c0486fd3cf1900fd151a9a23cf374c6a0ccec60ca47c64c3.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,2(x-2)^{2}-1\\le y\\le 2-(x-2)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{2(x-2)^{2}-1}^{2-(x-2)^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{2(x-2)^{2}-1}^{2-(x-2)^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80634/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e891363-fea2-5de4-9bbb-67fddb077200"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80634"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81340/selection/5d33d5c167577850046475475e367ad4315dacedf87ddcbcaec19649c325cf4e" :answer/id #uuid "da7686a3-9aa0-5d3d-bf87-66e146de1d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{1}[{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81340/selection/28dea20eb96b32c7645692d4f4f68099ff73d7c849fb36a1cc884e920c9966ef" :answer/id #uuid "a6e58716-e592-57fc-81c2-57636f3be1fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{1}[{\\int }_{3-{x}^{2}}^{x+1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81340/selection/32fef51ee4be78db6822d05c33bad0af8443355de9c854e10eab49eb5d4ac997" :answer/id #uuid "1eddb42c-76db-530e-913a-8cdb2bee43df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81340/selection/c4433d28f499dcdf1f7318dff5cd636e430930c197e2e56fcb800d6b00d8e52e" :answer/id #uuid "e2f9a85e-bc44-5b4f-bf49-b007718bc397" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[{\\int }_{3-{x}^{2}}^{x+1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81340/selection/880d3ff7c35d90d687db7d66a88fc450083ccb60d7917b7770fc673f8841a1be" :answer/id #uuid "285d8434-c927-5d41-bd36-54db2866c583" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81340/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e17de0b-4ac9-5cb9-93c5-360d939e0f07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81340/selection/5d33d5c167577850046475475e367ad4315dacedf87ddcbcaec19649c325cf4e" :answer-field/choices ["q-81340/selection/5d33d5c167577850046475475e367ad4315dacedf87ddcbcaec19649c325cf4e" "q-81340/selection/28dea20eb96b32c7645692d4f4f68099ff73d7c849fb36a1cc884e920c9966ef" "q-81340/selection/32fef51ee4be78db6822d05c33bad0af8443355de9c854e10eab49eb5d4ac997" "q-81340/selection/c4433d28f499dcdf1f7318dff5cd636e430930c197e2e56fcb800d6b00d8e52e" "q-81340/selection/880d3ff7c35d90d687db7d66a88fc450083ccb60d7917b7770fc673f8841a1be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81340" :question/id #uuid "449fcf8c-3af3-5e89-b45f-8866876cef67" :question/math-academy-id "q-81340" :question/problem "If $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=3-{x}^{2}$ and $y=x+1,$ then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/7316d667d7308ac5ec0f5348055d3d0e7eb90b97abaa74f5693c3151dc3b8bb1.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-{x}^{2} & =x+1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+x-2 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)(x+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$-2\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/aab6fb99694b518bfa9d200a75876c9e888ba1ab7d699464bc9caca360be775a.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 1,\\,x+1\\le y\\le 3-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}[{\\int }_{x+1}^{3-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81340/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "853b2770-5057-50aa-9c15-7426cf4cc6a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81340"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81336/selection/e333af465d69f8482c342899fcfc000a7c7be31ebf4949593c6d265753233bf7" :answer/id #uuid "5db8ef76-6ff4-5570-ad56-e6fcd7bcced6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81336/selection/5475cf7a34ed3aac44711430d2518412369de75d4494dcfd755ba92b2a6e5bd3" :answer/id #uuid "2d0075da-bb02-5284-9285-685f02ddfd6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81336/selection/63e0a5621b2c7ce85a0e35258f30fab0d01fa384057eff2939d0ab9a8316dced" :answer/id #uuid "53be0223-a426-59b3-b6d0-5b877713bdaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81336/selection/0a95acfeb2e68c44d8d9f7a551483b00b7464907835b6055f7e46f9731f8a1cb" :answer/id #uuid "55961f86-e2ca-5f26-86ab-0a274fd7466d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81336/selection/a3a9d867ad13fd5715468af244d3fa8796231857271052e167fc10dd14a6cb55" :answer/id #uuid "5a12ddb5-8fc9-53dd-95e9-4074236ed8af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81336/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e5f1ced-f2e4-5a3d-b419-5aa471935fa7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81336/selection/5475cf7a34ed3aac44711430d2518412369de75d4494dcfd755ba92b2a6e5bd3" :answer-field/choices ["q-81336/selection/e333af465d69f8482c342899fcfc000a7c7be31ebf4949593c6d265753233bf7" "q-81336/selection/5475cf7a34ed3aac44711430d2518412369de75d4494dcfd755ba92b2a6e5bd3" "q-81336/selection/63e0a5621b2c7ce85a0e35258f30fab0d01fa384057eff2939d0ab9a8316dced" "q-81336/selection/0a95acfeb2e68c44d8d9f7a551483b00b7464907835b6055f7e46f9731f8a1cb" "q-81336/selection/a3a9d867ad13fd5715468af244d3fa8796231857271052e167fc10dd14a6cb55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81336" :question/id #uuid "e08c75d3-95c8-54b4-9cdf-5e4550896e07" :question/math-academy-id "q-81336" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/c497efbb28bade962b997d7e14f5a272f0cead56f7567b1baaebae695c7c80f4.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the lines $y=e,$ $x=0,$ and the curve $y={e}^{x},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & =e \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/95a6d9b0bc464c719311dc900967ebd06a3aa3d3004cfe5303359eecb20551e7.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{e}^{x}\\le y\\le e}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{x}}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81336/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "853b2770-5057-50aa-9c15-7426cf4cc6a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81336"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40822/selection/6eaae2b6367f108872846d8b2075caf063de893e327a438b529d1a4c62133bd7" :answer/id #uuid "c0170f64-44a7-5ea7-a516-bb90f398b833" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{9-{x}^{2}}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40822/selection/398b3b3cbdd1b33c7e1a249ae12688fdd56a4a36f0d400457621f0744523a297" :answer/id #uuid "c621dc57-07cd-57d8-88f8-f91cc5efa0f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{9-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{2}^{9-{x}^{2}}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40822/selection/085532ce6e92195747dbd89a7b9a6ca238308071a58c4ef714e157a093db4b1c" :answer/id #uuid "e0f8aa78-f523-50db-a0dd-3011a3adb9c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40822/selection/19c8ef747ad00e0c960836628b30bf9c707c54f7bd99ed27fca2ebbe70f6d676" :answer/id #uuid "b83f6f8f-0f79-5637-9484-1a57f6448678" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{2}{\\int }_{9-{x}^{2}}^{2}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40822/selection/235bad6f16ad3bc7ff804472ee5e37393ee0d4bc3bd2162f6eaef31477fc0ca9" :answer/id #uuid "c3407904-204f-5610-89a4-319e6c5675b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{9-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40822/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "49c33087-f456-55d0-8f3e-3f3fb3b75c94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40822/selection/6eaae2b6367f108872846d8b2075caf063de893e327a438b529d1a4c62133bd7" :answer-field/choices ["q-40822/selection/6eaae2b6367f108872846d8b2075caf063de893e327a438b529d1a4c62133bd7" "q-40822/selection/398b3b3cbdd1b33c7e1a249ae12688fdd56a4a36f0d400457621f0744523a297" "q-40822/selection/085532ce6e92195747dbd89a7b9a6ca238308071a58c4ef714e157a093db4b1c" "q-40822/selection/19c8ef747ad00e0c960836628b30bf9c707c54f7bd99ed27fca2ebbe70f6d676" "q-40822/selection/235bad6f16ad3bc7ff804472ee5e37393ee0d4bc3bd2162f6eaef31477fc0ca9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40822" :question/id #uuid "26444f9e-45df-56c7-85ca-aa68ae575349" :question/math-academy-id "q-40822" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/933e68e42fe61af3e30fae012b0b56dce6793b0fadc343e04a0766b85cb6ae7e.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=9-{x}^{2}$ and $y=1+{x}^{2},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{x}^{2} & =9-{x}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$-2\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/c56c5be4ac88755f1859f295f700be8710d75b16380ac120e6b56a3aa767acbe.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,1+{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 9-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{9-{x}^{2}}(x{y}^{2}+2x)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40822/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "853b2770-5057-50aa-9c15-7426cf4cc6a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40822"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132249/selection/6998d764e25a6276c57b730edba40a63681b82e97b4ebad4b33671749eb6c31f" :answer/id #uuid "d631cab9-51ec-5be9-922c-27df2b638a6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2x}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{6-x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132249/selection/9324dbd253deeacb75c609960d9f79aaad963f15e24cfcaa78bff4995b61212e" :answer/id #uuid "27eeec87-782e-54c7-a56b-4c01e1ed47b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{6-x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132249/selection/2ba5f72e9ac595b86ca169a54ad2c4462f3dd6cabef9c085104f903f0b0d887a" :answer/id #uuid "6350f6c2-9f92-5c4c-97d6-5e2448bba003" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{2x}^{6-x}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132249/selection/cafaa0fcc5170bdc63e6436a2fe2e1d88059e98340a35d1baddcdb1b6378263b" :answer/id #uuid "acd70137-e347-5c5d-95b3-df1150dbd44c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{6-x}^{2x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132249/selection/0903440c569692199c90c0686d196a86175858c8fa057b742a1f921d4e7a0ba9" :answer/id #uuid "18ca71c1-6f8e-51e3-a1e4-0e376c9d298d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{6-x}{\\int }_{2x}^{2}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132249/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a27b813-547c-50ba-bc55-dc6da72f6616" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132249/selection/9324dbd253deeacb75c609960d9f79aaad963f15e24cfcaa78bff4995b61212e" :answer-field/choices ["q-132249/selection/6998d764e25a6276c57b730edba40a63681b82e97b4ebad4b33671749eb6c31f" "q-132249/selection/9324dbd253deeacb75c609960d9f79aaad963f15e24cfcaa78bff4995b61212e" "q-132249/selection/2ba5f72e9ac595b86ca169a54ad2c4462f3dd6cabef9c085104f903f0b0d887a" "q-132249/selection/cafaa0fcc5170bdc63e6436a2fe2e1d88059e98340a35d1baddcdb1b6378263b" "q-132249/selection/0903440c569692199c90c0686d196a86175858c8fa057b742a1f921d4e7a0ba9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132249" :question/id #uuid "bf1ebc54-3588-5672-a9a8-34aff8268c29" :question/math-academy-id "q-132249" :question/problem "If $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the lines $y=2x,$ $y=6-x,$ and $x=0,$ then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/24d3b93e82e88bb581eff3005687ae4ee3dc3ae0d6c25fbc26f72665042ae5c6.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+6 & =2x \\\\ 3x & =6 \\\\ x & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/af61865f54494840090351296e8a1c21446787ca0b273005e7bf9c2907585adb.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,2x\\le y\\le 6-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{6-x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132249/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "853b2770-5057-50aa-9c15-7426cf4cc6a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132249"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40825/selection/48167ff7a027223f46feaab053f65c335b65e65b9af5f49be46a5f901a01f678" :answer/id #uuid "4105562e-9fda-5f64-9503-73859ee88c62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1/x}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{4}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40825/selection/85351cbe967b3e28a04e19115a0216e8762c672b5b3e8907a9018b8cdcf5dc78" :answer/id #uuid "fcf43ad3-3934-53b0-9199-59bf033d3b4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1/x}^{\\sqrt{x}}{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40825/selection/5e45619908fa37ef4ab415e533a0b97ae1f2a124eba3e9e9178264c4974f74a4" :answer/id #uuid "dac141e2-e0ef-5ece-b263-cd7b381490d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{x}}{\\int }_{1/x}^{4}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40825/selection/97dafd83f8d9f948c81f44096aed9aca5d167ced052b083dee8bd21d5e12aeeb" :answer/id #uuid "dc860a45-2255-5fa7-847c-103eaf9fc358" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{1/x}{\\int }_{4}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40825/selection/8e00124bfda8cef535060e4875409d602760059aef47e48d05c195cf42e30e0b" :answer/id #uuid "d3df03e8-6638-538f-8eaf-4b218bac8683" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1/x}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40825/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "828c9cb9-208e-5e9c-8ad5-961a464d8d5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40825/selection/8e00124bfda8cef535060e4875409d602760059aef47e48d05c195cf42e30e0b" :answer-field/choices ["q-40825/selection/48167ff7a027223f46feaab053f65c335b65e65b9af5f49be46a5f901a01f678" "q-40825/selection/85351cbe967b3e28a04e19115a0216e8762c672b5b3e8907a9018b8cdcf5dc78" "q-40825/selection/5e45619908fa37ef4ab415e533a0b97ae1f2a124eba3e9e9178264c4974f74a4" "q-40825/selection/97dafd83f8d9f948c81f44096aed9aca5d167ced052b083dee8bd21d5e12aeeb" "q-40825/selection/8e00124bfda8cef535060e4875409d602760059aef47e48d05c195cf42e30e0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40825" :question/id #uuid "db42cd1f-0714-52f4-b27c-88e397059aec" :question/math-academy-id "q-40825" :question/problem "If $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=\\frac{1}{x},$ $y=\\sqrt{x},$ and $x=4,$ then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/fcb347767983c38eb12f521ca556dcc5a96705ee4e887fb8d43c42984dfe1a26.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x} & =\\sqrt{x} \\\\ x\\sqrt{x} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{x})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =1 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are \n$1\\le x\\le 4.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/91bf7087e5aa0053d24cb45158d48b0bb36fb84b28ebabaeba3c26dc62168dfe.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\frac{1}{x}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1/x}^{\\sqrt{x}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-40825/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "853b2770-5057-50aa-9c15-7426cf4cc6a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40825"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132277/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "0442ea3b-357d-53c8-b824-92b83b99af66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132277/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "4de1e23a-54d6-5496-b5d5-4c3bce83908e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132277/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "2f58a134-f50b-5fe2-a9f0-87ecefae3db2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132277/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "8bcdf6b2-ef20-50a1-b6f4-3eda07aa3e83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132277/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "6d5d30d8-9e52-526c-928c-97a1f45d1409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132277/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bca249b5-18bb-5137-b435-60045e37b197" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132277/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer-field/choices ["q-132277/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-132277/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-132277/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-132277/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-132277/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132277" :question/id #uuid "08c24ec0-e556-5a18-b494-94cb83244cbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-132277" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3x}{x}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[\\,y\\,]_{0}^{3x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(3x-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1)^{4}}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132277/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a28c4320-e2dd-5195-81ac-b910c2328691"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132277"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-37864"] :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}^{5}\\,dy\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}^{5}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}[y]_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}((1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\pi )^{6}}{6}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{32{\\pi }^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-37859/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "be5c6dfa-6bdf-5f84-bd4e-64e0ee52bdf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37859/selection/286a23b4f88ab5c5f58674d94dd3996a24158cd522f456ca4f7fa96ef4dc831e" :answer/id #uuid "12896bde-822e-572e-8ba6-a900187844b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37859/selection/bc1aaa9670e8118cdb6ca0d3888d99928c842323e3d10885fe212d998358f89d" :answer/id #uuid "5beb21d0-ed0c-51db-8b65-cb16c0d54ef8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37859/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" :answer/id #uuid "61faa33e-916b-5474-b93c-610240fdf96b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37859/selection/c2724874453e84fa99374647d0694dc238ab831bc6b7d897dc21c9d3c7e61851" :answer/id #uuid "0a521373-3750-550b-a832-f166caad32e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37859/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "089bfb55-638a-5b89-bc67-97e73646f13b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37859/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" :answer-field/choices ["q-37859/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-37859/selection/286a23b4f88ab5c5f58674d94dd3996a24158cd522f456ca4f7fa96ef4dc831e" "q-37859/selection/bc1aaa9670e8118cdb6ca0d3888d99928c842323e3d10885fe212d998358f89d" "q-37859/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" "q-37859/selection/c2724874453e84fa99374647d0694dc238ab831bc6b7d897dc21c9d3c7e61851"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37859" :question/id #uuid "890facf8-cfbe-521e-b890-2b14f7530e02" :question/math-academy-id "q-37859" :question/problem "${\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[{\\int }_{1/x}^{4x}y\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}([\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]_{1/x}^{4x})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(8{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}(8{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2x}]}_{1/2}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{1}{2})-(\\frac{1}{3}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37859/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a28c4320-e2dd-5195-81ac-b910c2328691"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37859"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132282/selection/b627bdd0369562afa8f12be8f167039ff5f7a2bdc550b832dce7f5205e0a89bc" :answer/id #uuid "81a72f17-9be5-5afc-bf91-23b9a4925a04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132282/selection/6d0086fbf1d5dadda84b813260fdcf9f8964549bf3d2a02972d43bc272b01425" :answer/id #uuid "1e3a7d85-670c-54ac-8adc-f2e426b9414c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132282/selection/aa76ea3c2bcf198aabf9b49d9f05d52d8f72c18a367ff0539bec41bc3dbc0f44" :answer/id #uuid "bd95ebcc-92f8-5f35-be91-fc86a601624b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132282/selection/f6cd7ad815cbceebfe1cddfb3219edf7d8bce0273da1c741fc6acf433fc7d1c8" :answer/id #uuid "51c9a413-b430-5ad6-bb11-aa3c70e869e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132282/selection/fbba2282d0f8beb03471ee9e51af677372e074f856fa626d26c85344c5591b6a" :answer/id #uuid "db59b8da-eda1-5e27-8cb7-7d91f47caf59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\pi }^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132282/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2065018f-7568-5c71-ba8f-86366d324240" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132282/selection/6d0086fbf1d5dadda84b813260fdcf9f8964549bf3d2a02972d43bc272b01425" :answer-field/choices ["q-132282/selection/b627bdd0369562afa8f12be8f167039ff5f7a2bdc550b832dce7f5205e0a89bc" "q-132282/selection/6d0086fbf1d5dadda84b813260fdcf9f8964549bf3d2a02972d43bc272b01425" "q-132282/selection/aa76ea3c2bcf198aabf9b49d9f05d52d8f72c18a367ff0539bec41bc3dbc0f44" "q-132282/selection/f6cd7ad815cbceebfe1cddfb3219edf7d8bce0273da1c741fc6acf433fc7d1c8" "q-132282/selection/fbba2282d0f8beb03471ee9e51af677372e074f856fa626d26c85344c5591b6a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132282" :question/id #uuid "a97d9c12-2933-5c3f-9e27-d7927fc2abf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-132282" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}4x\\,dx & ={[2{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132282/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a28c4320-e2dd-5195-81ac-b910c2328691"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132282"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81353/selection/a8e18a8c0c345a7537a155ca7d3f8784a0df5622e667f76d1252dc080a800bd4" :answer/id #uuid "0f0e826d-fd6d-55bd-9980-6ae826a5bc6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{32}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81353/selection/606aa2b4ebca78c0dd587b8d744cd343a49e004ba235c409987cb82383a6e58d" :answer/id #uuid "b1ee17b8-9e3c-568d-894f-6424f28d2d70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81353/selection/9b11f79ffefa4ece0a41d7dd2a9a8ddfcefcf5f2e6608498379340919307e4ea" :answer/id #uuid "3cfeaba2-72f7-58f2-a4b7-12a2b90d54d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{32}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81353/selection/8e1065e0a433f859a01c77631b6451e105d707d70e2225dc268d4aa4c9c23074" :answer/id #uuid "76fed0f5-613b-5ca3-bfd8-b4587065bca8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81353/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "b451b922-a443-5496-90f5-445f1fc87bad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81353/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d4aff28-90e7-5490-85ed-655b1c8653ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81353/selection/9b11f79ffefa4ece0a41d7dd2a9a8ddfcefcf5f2e6608498379340919307e4ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-81353/selection/a8e18a8c0c345a7537a155ca7d3f8784a0df5622e667f76d1252dc080a800bd4" "q-81353/selection/606aa2b4ebca78c0dd587b8d744cd343a49e004ba235c409987cb82383a6e58d" "q-81353/selection/9b11f79ffefa4ece0a41d7dd2a9a8ddfcefcf5f2e6608498379340919307e4ea" "q-81353/selection/8e1065e0a433f859a01c77631b6451e105d707d70e2225dc268d4aa4c9c23074" "q-81353/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81353" :question/id #uuid "edc91c22-9833-5005-b359-ebe6680861cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-81353" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-x}^{3x}\\sqrt{x+y}\\,dy\\,dx=$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-x}^{3x}\\sqrt{x+y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-x}^{3x}\\sqrt{x+y}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{2}{3}(x+y)^{3/2}]}_{-x}^{3x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{2}{3}(x+3x)^{3/2}-\\frac{2}{3}(x-x)^{3/2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2}{3}(4x)^{3/2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{3/2}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3/2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3/2}\\,dx & =\\frac{16}{3}{[\\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}(\\frac{2}{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81353/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a28c4320-e2dd-5195-81ac-b910c2328691"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81353"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81361/selection/f1beb35332f9c581dd32db6ff64ded64a93f76711bf8de469eb26617533404d6" :answer/id #uuid "ba04d36b-cc64-5596-abf1-39b10004c817" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{81}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81361/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer/id #uuid "a2d553ac-5023-5161-9df7-5eb06345acd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81361/selection/87c940e45a28f94969563df81faaf5ad4d2979643afd98f5c1058d45040cd06e" :answer/id #uuid "30d9b519-7bd1-5c7f-bafc-d32ed8255b21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{41}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81361/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "61d35717-a6a9-5f56-bb3a-fca125c6ff49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81361/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "d31a8b62-6efd-5c2d-970b-f351d78a549e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81361/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8999b79-b7e2-5458-9e43-8a90b6381570" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81361/selection/f1beb35332f9c581dd32db6ff64ded64a93f76711bf8de469eb26617533404d6" :answer-field/choices ["q-81361/selection/f1beb35332f9c581dd32db6ff64ded64a93f76711bf8de469eb26617533404d6" "q-81361/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" "q-81361/selection/87c940e45a28f94969563df81faaf5ad4d2979643afd98f5c1058d45040cd06e" "q-81361/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-81361/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81361" :question/id #uuid "559567ed-95bb-59d3-8c41-bbeb1f57531e" :question/math-academy-id "q-81361" :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{D}3x{e}^{y}\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over the type I region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}3x{e}^{y}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}3x{e}^{y}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}3x{e}^{y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{e}^{y}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x{[{e}^{y}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-{e}^{0})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x(x-1)dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(3{x}^{2}-3x)dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(3{x}^{2}-3x)dx & ={[{x}^{3}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =(64-24)-(1-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =40+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81361/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "69f6b2a7-7a3a-5c2c-90db-5aa321784048"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81361"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81367/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d7c92b1d-6b43-55a9-a71f-11970c5f0625" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81367/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "cf3883c4-12d8-5ea5-a315-aa689cd924af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81367/selection/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d" :answer/id #uuid "ac6196f7-aa5c-59c8-a2ed-636910f7f23d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81367/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" :answer/id #uuid "560f5905-6606-580e-9de0-d71c7203870a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81367/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "781c76d3-5ab5-5868-a72b-33b6cc12f6ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81367/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e76fe949-3a16-5799-9f0a-8c72c903f90d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81367/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-81367/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-81367/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-81367/selection/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d" "q-81367/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" "q-81367/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81367" :question/id #uuid "d2d78dc5-4a32-5648-b82a-d72069352571" :question/math-academy-id "q-81367" :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral\n${∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dA,$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the lines\n$x=e,$ $y=e$ and the curve $y={e}^{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/aa635ca5ef3198fea56d684b034de476a72e4ace2a4c51b37c6c59977036eb76.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- The line $y=e$ intercepts the curve $y={e}^{x}$ at $x=1.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$1\\le x\\le e.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/b78021a06c9fea100b75c66a619c425345cda3666d84da018895be15a53af06d.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,e\\le y\\le {e}^{x}}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dA={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}[{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)]}_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{x})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx & ={[\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡x}{2}]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡e}{2}-\\frac{{ln}^{2}⁡1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-81367/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "69f6b2a7-7a3a-5c2c-90db-5aa321784048"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81367"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-37863"] :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dA,\\,$ where $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over the type I region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le x}.$ \n\nSo, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)]_{0}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-81778/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "9d00f5d4-c41f-54b8-beb0-4c8f4b747015" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81778/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "c5a80775-a3c4-5884-a236-b3347a3ad076" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81778/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "694dbd39-e9e5-5202-85e9-3bea2eed4694" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81778/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "189d7840-f007-5050-9d50-f784f644336b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81778/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225" :answer/id #uuid "debc78b2-2cae-52bc-aff9-feeb3f73a9a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81778/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4049ac91-059a-5523-9978-55599f7ad46d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81778/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-81778/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-81778/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-81778/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-81778/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-81778/selection/29e18d29d5a8d00489a807deb821c9d8fb2c816d74392c4ec1d541f26b369225"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81778" :question/id #uuid "4ceba7fa-2b80-52a5-88ca-4755634a6025" :question/math-academy-id "q-81778" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/786dd06154d1bda5483ed992dce8922c9629f759b498a3f713c35612311c1ee6.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,dA,$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region below the line $y=2$ enclosed by the lines $y=x$ and $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- We already know the intersection of the line $y=x$ with the line $y=2.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$0\\le x\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/92b1eda4ccf9e62e1f7310b1ba9bef5cc6c434755e74196d1829a30f2c4a3c53.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,x\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{8x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{12}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{4}{3}-0 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81778/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "69f6b2a7-7a3a-5c2c-90db-5aa321784048"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81778"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81774/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "9b24122c-932c-5f2a-899b-4fd0f9a5d968" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81774/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "00ac95fe-8fb6-55aa-9544-d198a90bc26c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81774/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "c97effbb-0df8-5a30-b6f1-ead0cdc253a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81774/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "f2f9f392-a139-5101-aa87-79cba5753cb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81774/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9094a929-555a-5774-8dc6-b669377219c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81774/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f42acf4b-c19b-56c6-9624-af0deeb49ad5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81774/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer-field/choices ["q-81774/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-81774/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-81774/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-81774/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-81774/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81774" :question/id #uuid "a3dc511f-22f2-5e83-aeb1-3756802568a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-81774" :question/problem "Calculate ${∬}_{D}x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over the type I region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}x\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}x\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[y]_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x({x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(1-{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{3})dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{3})dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81774/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "69f6b2a7-7a3a-5c2c-90db-5aa321784048"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81774"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7024"] :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $x=0,$ $y=0,$ and the curve $y=\\sqrt{4 - x^2}.$ What is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D (x+y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/3d67d73d3ede011d6c2fe4bc9e160aa3c2af522bff6cddfcc7c351c97418e764.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq 2, \\quad 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt{4-x^2} \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}(x+y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7025"] :question/problem "If $D$ is the finite region in the first quadrant enclosed by the curves $y=3x$ and $y=x^3,$ then what is $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} f\\left( {x,y} \\right) \\, \\mathrm{d}A$ expressed as a repeated integral?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/f8a5fd7fc3e98d7f08b5ea48636e5de4a1a45b7a94fbe9e968789afcfe3a582c.png)\n\nNow, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. \n\n- To determine the $x$-limits, we need to find the $x$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =3x \\\\ {x}^{3}-3x & =0 \\\\ x({x}^{2}-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $x$-limits are $0 \\le x \\le \\sqrt{3}.$ Note that we disregarded the solution $x=-\\sqrt 3$ since $x\\geq 0$ in our region.\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/232f885d2230694bf62f81f5987cd2b3a12a49430d90d2cae4712c552587a48c.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq \\sqrt{3}, \\quad x^3 \\leq y \\leq 3x \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{3x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}[{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{3x}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7026"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 \\int_0^x x^2y \\,\\textrm{d}y \\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{5}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7027"] :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}A,\\:$\nwhere $D$ is the finite region below the $x$-axis enclosed by the circle $x^2 + y^2 = 4.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $y \\leq 0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx^2 + y^2 = 4\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\ny = -\\sqrt{4-x^2}.\n$$\n\nLet's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/31e7bb281a36a3676730de0883d7abd5445093713de1bbd41899cce50a7e0e48.png)\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region.\n\n- We already know the intersection of the circle with the line $y=0.$\nSo, the $x$-limits are \n$-2 \\le x \\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14054607/assets/2a84d17b83fb1e2036c6edc0a71c5c10a58bf893c33bbf38662ebb417aab3164.png)\n\nAs a result, the integral is defined over the following type I region: \n\n$$\nD = \\Big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\quad -\\sqrt{4-x^2} \\leq y \\leq 0 \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iint \\limits_{D} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}A = \\int_{-2}^2 \\int_{-\\sqrt{4-x^2}}^{0} xy\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}^{0}xy\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}x[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}^{0}y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}^{0}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x(0-(-\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}})^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x(-(4-{x}^{2}))\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}x({x}^{2}-4)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{3}-4x)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{3}-4x)\\,dx & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-2{x}^{2}]}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((4-8)-(4-8)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
